zebez@home.se (zebez) wrote:

> I'm just curious as of why the windows tty creates a 25x80 console
> window, and not a 24x80? With a 25x80 console window it creates a
> scrollbar and an empty blank line at the bottom of the window.
> It's very easy to change it in the source file  sys\winnt\nttty.c
> , so it creates a 24x80 window. I have tested it a little and see
> no apparent negative effects. Anyone know if there is a good
> reason? 

80x24 is the size of a VT100 terminal. 80x25 is the size of an IBM PC 
terminal. If you enter full-screen mode on a PC, the terminal you get 
will be 80x25 regardless, and almost every way of creating terminals in 
WinNT defaults to 80x25. So why go out of the way to break the 
convention? If you want an 80x24 terminal to run NetHack in, you can 
easily make one yourself without having to modify NH.

